  "body": "Found in the review read of PR #3618 (#3361). Refs #3567, #3577.\n\n**Background:** in 2D, a later Outside pass that starts in a dead end entered by a helix into uncut stock (#3567; PR #3577 gives it a ramp). 3D pocket now uses the same ring order for Inside and Outside.\n\n**What the read found:** in 3D a later ring has no helix. A centre-cutting tool plunges straight at the ring start, as the Auto order does today. A tool that does not cut at the centre goes through the plunge law (a helix, a ramp, or a refusal by name). So the result is a heavy plunge at worst, not a gouge. No test shows it.\n\n**Wanted:** a fixture with a 3D pocket level whose Outside order gives a later ring that starts in a closed area of uncut stock. Read the load at that entry, and compare it with the Auto ring-start plunge. If the load is larger, give the entry the ramp of #3577 or report it as a finding.\n\n**Done when:** a pin states the entry type and its load for that case.\n",
